You can also see how lme4 underestimates the variance of the group-level
effects compared to full Bayes.

And this

>> for (i in 1:1000)
>>   mu[i] <-  intercept + sigma * groupvar_raw[group[i]];

I'm pretty sure would be more efficient (certainly in terms of space)
than:

  for (i in 1:1000)

    mu[i] <- groupvar_raw[group[i]];
  mu <- intercept + sigma * mu;

I'm not sure how the new RStanARM is going to implement this but
it's something to keep in mind.

- Bob

