another possibility I have thought about is to simple make the intercept in the design matrix larger.
lets say the regression weight for the intercept regressor, which consists only of ones,
is two orders of magnitude larger than all other regressors (i.e. around 1 vs. around .01).
If one then simply uses an intercept regressor consisting of hundreds,
its regression weight will become 2 orders of magnitude smaller and have a similar scale as the other regression weights.

Does this make sense?

Guido

