I see that I was confused in thinking the x values were data.

still, the statement:

diff ~ lognormal(foo,bar)

is a statement about x[i,3] because x[i,3] *is* diff, so there is no transformation, only a deterministic connection between the value of x[i,3] and some other things that are known conditionally. If you were going to do

log(diff) ~ normal(...) for example, you'd need a jacobian correction.

at least, that's how I read it. I admit to being a little distracted at the moment, so hopefully Geoff will delve deeper to confirm as needed.

